00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:39.761
- [Voiceover] Jeanluc asks,
"This questions really

00:02:39.761 --> 00:02:41.054
"got me thinking.

00:02:41.054 --> 00:02:43.511
"When do you shift from
hiring a freelancer

00:02:43.511 --> 00:02:45.664
"to hiring someone for full time?"

00:02:47.444 --> 00:02:50.412
- Jeanluc, easy question.

00:02:50.412 --> 00:02:51.967
It's just easy.

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:53.531
There's really a couple of scenarios.

00:02:53.531 --> 00:02:56.335
Number one, the moment
you fall in love with them

00:02:56.335 --> 00:02:58.427
and you say you should
join my team full time

00:02:58.427 --> 00:03:00.418
because we're going to be great together,

00:03:00.418 --> 00:03:01.902
this well bring value to my business.

00:03:01.902 --> 00:03:04.238
Number two, when you have a necessity.

00:03:04.238 --> 00:03:06.351
When you're business is growing,

00:03:06.351 --> 00:03:07.935
whether it's a new
client or you're selling

00:03:07.935 --> 00:03:09.723
more of your stuff that
they're producing for

00:03:09.723 --> 00:03:10.821
or whatever it may be.

00:03:10.821 --> 00:03:12.284
Your business has grown

00:03:12.284 --> 00:03:14.701
and now you have a tested employee

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:17.444
that goes to full time.

00:03:17.444 --> 00:03:19.354
There's a third scenario when

00:03:19.354 --> 00:03:22.076
the freelancer is so infatuated with love

00:03:22.076 --> 00:03:24.311
with your business that
they're pushing aggressively

00:03:24.311 --> 00:03:25.509
to join the team.

00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:27.968
It may not be practical,
you may not be able

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:30.629
to fully afford it, but
your intuition tells you

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:33.209
that long term, you know
nine months from now,

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:34.550
the ROI will start kicking in

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:38.452
and I want to reward this
person's passion around me

00:03:38.452 --> 00:03:41.073
so I'm willing to make a little
less money in the short term

00:03:41.073 --> 00:03:44.466
for that relationship and that
stickiness of the long game.

00:03:44.466 --> 00:03:48.001
Those tend to be the
scenarios when you make

00:03:48.001 --> 00:03:50.579
the shift, Jeanluc.

